    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0218" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg184"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sherman to Baron
                            von Thielmann.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the Department’s note
                    to you of the 10th instant, offering on behalf of this Government to extend
                    protection and render assistance at St. Pierre, Martinique, to Captain Aim,
                    master of the German bark <hi rendition="#italic">Elisabeth Ahrens</hi>, and to
                    your reply thereto of the same date, I have the honor to inform you that upon
                    receipt of your communication a telegram in the sense of my above-mentioned note
                    was at once sent to the American consul at Martinique.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Sherman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
